I don't post those very often, but here's a very unlucky one.

The major event in the life of this elven wizard was finding
a double (or triple) bones file of previous lucky wizards,
getting lots of scrolls, wands, potions, etc. It took me a
lot of running around (to minetown, the only altar) before
I could identify and uncurse everything.  Once this was
done, I thought this is going to be a good game.  AC went
down to -23, I had Magicbane, etc.  I read some [s] YAAPs
and I liked the idea of robbing One Eyed Sam by polying
into a xorn.  That's how the YASD began.

So I went there, gathered a lot of loot, put it all into 2
bags, polyed and went out.  That part was easy.  BUT,
as I was teleported back to the dungeon, I found myself
sorrounded by some rather nasty creatures (from all
sides), like a soldier, a deep one, etc.  These aren't VERY
nasty creatures, but nasty enough to kill a stressed
xorn very quickly.  After which I turned into an elf with 20
hp, NAKED, OVERTAXED.  I'd zap that wand of teleportation,
but I was overtaxed, I'd read a ?oTele, but no.  I don't know
if I could engrave with magicbane (thought about it later).
Anyway, I drank a potion of extra healing, which gave me
9 hp. Thanks.  Next round I was dead.

So, where did all the monsters come from?  They all
spawned in the corridor behind the market, and then
marched into the portal as I was sorting the loot.  I
couldn't have forseen that.  Another lesson learned, 
leave Sam alone.



